1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:02,120
<i>It was February 19th,</i>

2
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:04,440
<i>with Valentine's Day fever
still fresh in the air.</i>

3
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:10,600
<i>Soon, it'd be three months since I'd last 
managed to get in touch with Mizuhara.</i>

4
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:50,360
I thought I was good at going it alone

5
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:50,360
Would you prefer to go together?

6
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:17,890
Place
your finger here

7
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:39,030
Rent-a-Girlfriend

8
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:45,420
Heya! Some yoga pamphlet addressed to you got delivered
to me instead. Should I slip it through your mail slot?

9
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:45,420
Read

10
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:49,420
"Valentine's and Girlfriend"

11
00:01:48,190 --> 00:01:51,170
<i>She probably has me blocked.</i>

12
00:01:52,130 --> 00:01:55,420
<i>I feel so stupid, 
staring at this chat log forever!</i>

13
00:01:55,420 --> 00:02:01,390
<i>Wait, I've heard that you can try gifting 
stickers to see if you've been blocked.</i>

14
00:02:01,390 --> 00:02:21,500
You can't send this gift

15
00:02:01,390 --> 00:02:21,500
blush

16
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:05,610
A hidden feature that will 
only lead you to hell.

17
00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:11,210
If you try to gift someone a 
sticker set and it won't let you,

18
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:21,500
But it'd be best to not find
yourself in a situation where
you have to resort to this

19
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:21,500
Try this with a set you're
absolutely sure they wouldn't have ♥

20
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:16,640
that means they either have you 
blocked or already own that set.

21
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:21,160
The original creator also tried this out, 
and the app wouldn't let him.

22
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:29,840
Fiery Man Sticker Set

23
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:29,840
Pretty Please

24
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:25,330
<i>But I'll never recover if it turns out 
she does have me blocked.</i>

25
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:29,840
I wanna know

26
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:29,540
<i>That'd mean I'm just a guy she wants 
to forget and move on from.</i>

27
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:29,840
I don't wanna know

28
00:02:27,790 --> 00:02:29,840
But I
wanna know

29
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:33,180
<i>Maybe she's already with some other guy!</i>

30
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:35,320
Are you texting any other guys?

31
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,930
I've got my hands full with you.

32
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:43,810
blood

33
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:41,070
Ugh! I opened Pandora's Box again!

34
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:43,810
Is my brain sentient?!
This is just self-harm!!

35
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:43,810
How many times must I hurt 
myself before I'm satisfied?!

36
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:45,730
Ichinose Chizuru

37
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:45,730
Are you sure you want to gift this?

38
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:52,280
I did it

39
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,280
<i>Phew. She hasn't blocked me.</i>

40
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:52,280
I made it to the
confirm screen...

41
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:55,780
<i>She is still ghosting me, though.</i>

42
00:02:55,320 --> 00:03:01,490
What am I even doing

43
00:02:55,780 --> 00:03:01,150
<i>How I'd love it if she said she was 
digital detoxing for three months.</i>

44
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:01,490
That doesn't explain her
pretending not to be home

45
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:03,450
You sent a gift.

46
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:03,450
Read

47
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:03,450
Hmm?

48
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:10,290
I gifted it!!

49
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:10,290
Come back!!

50
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:10,290
Come back
to me!!

51
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:05,600
Gah! I fat-fingered!

52
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:10,290
I'm some weirdo who gifts a sticker set 
after being ghosted for three months!

53
00:03:17,590 --> 00:03:18,670
Time to kill myself.

54
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,580
Yes?

55
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:26,640
Oh, it's just you. What's up?

56
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:29,020
snort

57
00:03:29,810 --> 00:03:31,480
Raging bull...

58
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:33,480
What?

59
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,070
Ruka-chan?

60
00:03:35,070 --> 00:03:36,920
That's what she told me.

61
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:43,410
She also said she feels bad
for doing this to you

62
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,220
Even though she pushed 
you two to get together,

63
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:43,410
she was wishy-washy for so long, 
but now she wants to make things right.

64
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,620
<i>That's what Mizuhara was thinking?</i>

65
00:03:47,070 --> 00:03:49,460
<i>So she doesn't hate me or anything!</i>

66
00:03:49,970 --> 00:03:53,880
But frankly, I didn't get 
anything concrete from her.

67
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:58,840
If she knew how you felt, 
she'd give you an answer of some sort.

68
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:01,680
That's what the Mizuhara-san 
I know would've done.

69
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:06,230
She also said she doesn't know what 
to call the feelings she has for you

70
00:04:06,230 --> 00:04:07,430
that made her kiss you.

71
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,600
<i>Yeah, she knew I was trying 
to ask her out, too.</i>

72
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,860
<i>She did all that knowing how I felt!</i>

73
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:19,270
I'm simple-minded, so I believe nobody 
kisses someone they don't like.

74
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:18,610
Just personally speaking

75
00:04:19,270 --> 00:04:24,080
But if she says she's not sure, 
I can't really say anything to her.

76
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:24,080
I did what I could

77
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,290
Hmm? Master?

78
00:04:30,290 --> 00:04:34,680
I'm so glad. So she doesn't hate me now.

79
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:36,760
<i>Sheesh, this guy.</i>

80
00:04:37,590 --> 00:04:39,220
Thank you, Yaemori-san!

81
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:41,550
S-Sure!

82
00:04:41,930 --> 00:04:44,260
I'll go talk to her!

83
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:48,850
All this time, I've thought 
she rejected me.

84
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:50,360
I'm sorry.

85
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:54,450
I thought she thought I was a pain,

86
00:04:54,450 --> 00:04:56,340
and the kiss meant nothing at all.

87
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:59,790
These past three months, I've been 
telling myself she'd come to hate me.

88
00:05:00,190 --> 00:05:04,510
But I was wrong. 
Nothing could make me happier.

89
00:05:05,110 --> 00:05:09,600
This was rock bottom. 
Things can only go up from here.

90
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,580
If she knows how I feel, 
then I'd like an answer from her.

91
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:17,550
I'll try to hear how Mizuhara 
feels straight from her!

92
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:24,860
That's it! That's the spirit!

93
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:25,550
Yep!

94
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:28,770
You're looking like
a main character now

95
00:05:25,990 --> 00:05:27,770
I'm cheering for you with all my heart!

96
00:05:26,850 --> 00:05:28,770
Good luck with
your cosplays, too

97
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:28,770
Thanks!

98
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:32,090
<i>Resolve and resignation are 
two sides of the same coin,</i>

99
00:05:32,090 --> 00:05:34,650
<i>but both always take lots of courage.</i>

100
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,280
How do I get it
out of her?

101
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:39,280
<i>Well, what now?</i>

102
00:05:39,590 --> 00:05:43,050
<i>Should I text her an apology 
for gifting her a weird sticker set?</i>

103
00:05:43,050 --> 00:05:46,090
<i>Or should I go ring her doorbell again?</i>

104
00:05:46,090 --> 00:05:49,750
<i>If I knock on her door and call out 
to her, surely she can't still ignore me.</i>

105
00:05:50,150 --> 00:05:54,630
<i>But the fact is, she ghosted me 
because she felt bad for Ruka-chan.</i>

106
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:58,380
Like our values
don't agree
or something

107
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:58,830
<i>She might think I'm wrong for 
trying to barge in on her after that.</i>

108
00:06:03,550 --> 00:06:05,550
Rental Girlfriend Agency

109
00:06:03,550 --> 00:06:05,550
Kinoshita Kazuya-sama, your date
with Mizuhara Chizuru has
been confirmed!

110
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:05,550
Hey, I got it!

111
00:06:05,550 --> 00:06:07,080
Mizuhara okayed a date with me!

112
00:06:05,550 --> 00:06:07,510
We managed to confirm the schedule with the girlfriend you picked, so the date will proceed according to your booking.

113
00:06:09,550 --> 00:06:12,950
<i>What's going on? Is that confirmation 
she doesn't hate me?</i>

114
00:06:12,950 --> 00:06:15,060
<i>Did something change with Mizuhara?</i>

115
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:19,780
<i>But a rental date, huh? I guess 
that'd make it easier for her, too.</i>

116
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,740
<i>I see. Makes sense.</i>

117
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,280
<i>Renting is how it all started, 
so we go back to it.</i>

118
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:28,240
<i>Mizuhara...</i>

119
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,000
<i>Mizuhara!</i>

120
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:33,370
March 1

121
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:33,370
Harajuku

122
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,500
Cleaned up

123
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:47,090
<i>Gah, I can't! My head's about to 
explode from all the nerves!</i>

124
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:47,090
Here we have a virgin
holding his head
in Japan's trendiest town

125
00:06:47,430 --> 00:06:50,560
<i>I'm seeing Mizuhara for the 
first time in three months!</i>

126
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,660
<i>Will I even be able to talk to her?</i>

127
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,020
Uh, I'm sorry.

128
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:55,700
Nah, I'm sorry.

129
00:06:55,390 --> 00:07:00,110
A date that's
not the least bit fun

130
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:57,740
No, I should be the one apologizing.

131
00:06:57,740 --> 00:06:59,980
No, no, it should be me.

132
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:02,940
<i>This is probably gonna be 
awkward for her, too.</i>

133
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:05,430
<i>If I spoil the mood by asking 
her why she ghosted me,</i>

134
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:07,240
<i>it's gonna suck for both of us.</i>

135
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:11,810
<i>Did she choose to go on a rental date 
out of consideration for Ruka-chan again?</i>

136
00:07:11,290 --> 00:07:14,830
Over meeting outside work

137
00:07:11,810 --> 00:07:14,830
<i>That would add up with 
what Yaemori-san said.</i>

138
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:19,670
<i>But that still means she's willing 
to talk things out with me.</i>

139
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,590
<i>What will we even talk about?</i>

140
00:07:22,590 --> 00:07:25,210
<i>About her pretending to be out? 
About ignoring my messages?</i>

141
00:07:25,210 --> 00:07:26,180
<i>Or maybe...</i>

142
00:07:26,570 --> 00:07:28,680
She doesn't know what to call...

143
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,450
It's all good! I made reservations!

144
00:07:31,310 --> 00:07:37,100
I called ahead
to check

145
00:07:31,710 --> 00:07:32,870
What's with that guy?

146
00:07:32,310 --> 00:07:37,100
I even familiarized
myself with the area

147
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:34,620
Fresh off the boat?

148
00:07:33,450 --> 00:07:37,100
And I checked out the route there! 
There'll be plenty of time to chat!

149
00:07:37,630 --> 00:07:41,570
<i>But either way, we're about to 
reach some kind of conclusion.</i>

150
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:43,610
<i>If she's not sure how she feels,</i>

151
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:49,990
Just think about it

152
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:45,570
<i>there's still a chance
she might reject me.</i>

153
00:07:45,570 --> 00:07:49,990
<i>It's plenty likely that she'll just 
decide she doesn't feel that way.</i>

154
00:07:45,610 --> 00:07:49,990
This is Mizuhara and
me we're talking about

155
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:55,450
<i>But rejection doesn't scare me! 
Not anymore!</i>

156
00:08:04,670 --> 00:08:05,590
Hey.

157
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,340
<i>Sh-She's here!</i>

158
00:08:06,630 --> 00:08:08,340
It's Mizuhara

159
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:10,940
<i>It's Mizuhara! Right on time!</i>

160
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:13,010
It's Mizuhara

161
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:13,010
<i>She's right there, 
for the first time in three months!</i>

162
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:13,010
It's Mizuhara

163
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:13,010
She's so pretty

164
00:08:13,010 --> 00:08:18,100
<i>Wait, what do I lead with? 
Hello? Long time no see?</i>

165
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:23,480
Shall we head to the café?

166
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:28,530
Business as usual?!

167
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:27,960
<i>What?!</i>

168
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:28,530
So many people here. 
That's Harajuku, I guess.

169
00:08:26,990 --> 00:08:28,530
It amazes me every time

170
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:31,240
The new station building's so swanky.

171
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:31,320
<i>What? Wait, what?</i>

172
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:34,120
I liked the old one and its 
retro vibe, but this is nice, too.

173
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:34,120
<i>Huh? What?</i>

174
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:37,080
<i>She... She's acting totally normal!</i>

175
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:39,970
<i>Are you kidding me? How is that possible?</i>

176
00:08:37,450 --> 00:08:42,160
Sign of the times, I guess. 
The world keeps changing.

177
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:41,120
blasé

178
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:44,170
unaffected

179
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:44,170
<i>How can she meet me for the first time 
in months and act like nothing happened?!</i>

180
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:44,170
Whatever the reasoning

181
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:47,220
<i>Wait, am I the problem?!</i>

182
00:08:45,210 --> 00:08:47,630
My brain's about to fry...

183
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,630
What? Aren't we going?

184
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:51,840
Oh, yeah, let's go.

185
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,840
I was spacing out

186
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:54,160
She doesn't know what to call...

187
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:56,270
Yaemori-san
said all that

188
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:56,270
<i>No, that can't be!</i>

189
00:08:56,710 --> 00:08:59,190
<i>But we're on a rental date right now.</i>

190
00:08:59,190 --> 00:09:03,230
<i>Maybe she finds it awkward to bring 
up personal stuff right now, too.</i>

191
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:03,230
That makes sense

192
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:05,730
I'm glad it's nice and warm out.

193
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:09,600
<i>I mean, yeah, 
it's certainly not a fun topic.</i>

194
00:09:06,210 --> 00:09:08,540
I looked up the restaurant 
because I was so excited.

195
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:13,530
<i>As a pro, she might not want to do 
it right away and spoil the mood.</i>

196
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:13,530
Are we gonna talk
about it later, then?

197
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:17,540
<i>But who knows when 
we'll actually get to it?</i>

198
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:20,750
<i>She's gotta be looking for the right 
time to broach the topic, too.</i>

199
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:24,360
<i>Today... It's gotta be today!</i>

200
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:26,460
<i>I'll get it out of her during this date!</i>

201
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,670
<i>I have to know how she feels!</i>

202
00:09:29,530 --> 00:09:31,080
I'll lead the way.

203
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:32,130
Follow me

204
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,130
Yeah?

205
00:09:47,510 --> 00:09:49,440
What a pretty little café!

206
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,700
The perfect spot for afternoon tea!

207
00:09:52,210 --> 00:09:54,360
D-Do you come here often?

208
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:57,280
For afternoon tea? 
It's my first time here.

209
00:09:57,790 --> 00:10:01,000
<i>We should be able to have 
a nice, long chat here.</i>

210
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:01,000
We have an hour 
and a half

211
00:10:01,510 --> 00:10:05,690
This is your table. 
What will you have for drinks?

212
00:10:05,690 --> 00:10:07,610
I'll take Earl Grey.

213
00:10:07,610 --> 00:10:09,090
C-Coffee for me, please.

214
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,480
<i>She really is acting like 
nothing happened, though.</i>

215
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:17,090
<i>I'm starting to think Yaemori-san 
made all that up in her head.</i>

216
00:10:17,090 --> 00:10:20,750
<i>But y'know, I'd expect a 
"Sorry for ghosting you," at least.</i>

217
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:25,690
<i>But remember, we're on a rental date. 
Can't bring up personal lives here.</i>

218
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:25,690
Am I expecting too much?
2nd go-around

219
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:27,770
<i>And damn, Mizuhara...</i>

220
00:10:28,050 --> 00:10:30,250
<i>She's as pretty as ever today!</i>

221
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,820
<i>She has that versatile glow 
that doesn't fade</i>

222
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:39,740
Don't ask me why,
but that white sweater
goes hard!!

223
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:35,670
<i>or stick out in a fancy place like this.</i>

224
00:10:35,670 --> 00:10:39,740
Ooh, sakura mont blanc and sakura monaka? 
You can taste the spring coming!

225
00:10:35,670 --> 00:10:36,850
<i>If she steps out,</i>

226
00:10:36,850 --> 00:10:39,740
<i>she's a classy girl who doesn't look 
out of place in swanky Omotesando!</i>

227
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:43,910
<i>That white sweater plus coat is 
max sweetness and femininity,</i>

228
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:46,710
<i>and she has the hots 
to effortlessly pull it off.</i>

229
00:10:46,710 --> 00:10:50,210
<i>That slightly short skirt 
she only shows off indoors</i>

230
00:10:50,210 --> 00:10:52,670
<i>is like a bonus track from the heavens!</i>

231
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:57,390
<i>This girl and I really did kiss, huh?</i>

232
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:02,600
Here's today's special, the sakura 
and strawberry afternoon tea set.

233
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:04,940
Wow, that looks amazing!

234
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:04,940
Whoa...

235
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,970
<i>Don't be impressed! 
I need to broach the topic quick!</i>

236
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:08,080
We'll just
end up eating

237
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:12,110
A sip

238
00:11:11,470 --> 00:11:12,110
Want some?

239
00:11:13,890 --> 00:11:14,820
May I?

240
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:18,600
Not every day we have the chance. 
Might as well taste everything.

241
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:22,820
<i>Now we get a kiss of the indirect variety.</i>

242
00:11:22,370 --> 00:11:24,790
Maybe I'll
order it, too

243
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:24,160
Hey, this is great.

244
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:24,790
It's all-you-can-drink

245
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:24,790
Right?

246
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,670
<i>No! Not like this!</i>

247
00:11:26,670 --> 00:11:28,130
<i>Focus on the talk!</i>

248
00:11:28,430 --> 00:11:31,090
Mm, the quiche is so good!

249
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,510
<i>The talk!</i>

250
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:37,600
The crunch cake is out of this world, too.

251
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,720
I might actually really 
like the sakura flavor.

252
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:49,690
I can't stop
thinking about
her lips!!

253
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:55,950
<i>Heh... I went the whole hour 
and a half without bringing it up.</i>

254
00:11:52,570 --> 00:11:56,650
Thanks for
the treat ♥

255
00:11:53,570 --> 00:11:57,990
All I did

256
00:11:53,570 --> 00:11:55,900
was enjoy this
classy moment in time

257
00:11:55,570 --> 00:11:57,990
Today's Receipt:
Base Fee/hr 6,000 yen
Choice Fee (Regular) 5,000 yen
Traveling Costs 2,000 yen
Afternoon Tea 4,980 yen x 2 = 9,960 yen
Total: 28,960 yen

258
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:04,830
<i>There's 30 minutes left on this date. 
Can I really do this?</i>

259
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:07,330
<i>But if Yaemori-san's telling the truth,</i>

260
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:10,670
<i>that means Mizuhara's 
trying to avoid the topic, right?</i>

261
00:12:10,670 --> 00:12:14,870
<i>It's gotta be because she doesn't want to 
bring personal matters into a rental date.</i>

262
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:17,100
<i>But if not now, then when?</i>

263
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:20,090
<i>If I let this slip, will I even get a 
chance to talk it out with her again?</i>

264
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,010
<i>Yeah, I really can't let today end</i>

265
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:24,290
<i>without making things clear
one way or another!</i>

266
00:12:24,290 --> 00:12:26,240
<i>I came here expecting the worst, anyway!</i>

267
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:28,980
<i>If we're gonna talk, 
better sooner than later!</i>

268
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:32,940
It's only a matter of time before 
the fortress falls! No, it <i>wants</i> to fall!

269
00:12:33,350 --> 00:12:37,570
<i>I don't want to regret not saying 
anything here for the rest of my life!</i>

270
00:12:38,230 --> 00:12:41,480
<i>Go, me! Go for it!</i>

271
00:12:42,990 --> 00:12:44,990
Rent-a-Girlfriend

272
00:12:46,290 --> 00:12:49,710
Where we split up

273
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:48,460
Is the station good?

274
00:12:47,290 --> 00:12:49,710
That's the plan

275
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,710
Y-Yeah.

276
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:53,200
We have some time left. 
Let's hang around here.

277
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,370
O-Okay.

278
00:12:55,310 --> 00:12:58,430
<i>The clock's ticking down!</i>

279
00:12:56,340 --> 00:13:00,510
I hate how pathetic I am!!

280
00:12:58,430 --> 00:13:01,520
<i>But it's too late to bring it up now!</i>

281
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:06,650
<i>Mizuhara was the same as usual 
from start to end...</i>

282
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:09,600
Just the usual,
super-pretty Mizuhara

283
00:13:06,650 --> 00:13:09,600
<i>Maybe she only okayed this date on a whim?</i>

284
00:13:06,810 --> 00:13:09,600
sparkle♥

285
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:14,650
<i>Yaemori-san must've made up the part 
about her knowing how I feel.</i>

286
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:14,650
I believe
nothing

287
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:19,660
<i>This is who I am. 
This is who I'll always be.</i>

288
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:24,370
<i>Whenever I see Mizuhara, her beauty 
overwhelms me and breaks my brain.</i>

289
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:27,330
You're a really nice guy, huh?

290
00:13:27,330 --> 00:13:29,600
<i>I may say I'm not afraid of anything,</i>

291
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:32,900
<i>but when I see her smile, the idea 
of her scorning me terrifies me</i>

292
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:36,170
<i>and leaves me forever unable to 
take that step. Same old, same old.</i>

293
00:13:36,790 --> 00:13:41,010
<i>I'm your typical "nice guy." 
Nothing more than that.</i>

294
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:42,800
Here.

295
00:14:00,050 --> 00:14:00,900
Chocolate.

296
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,260
For you.

297
00:14:09,570 --> 00:14:11,890
H-Hey, thanks.

298
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:16,610
<i>Wait, what? Ch-Ch-Chocolate?</i>

299
00:14:16,610 --> 00:14:20,660
<i>Valentine's was two weeks ago. 
She's been wanting to give me this?</i>

300
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:22,150
<i>What does it mean?</i>

301
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:24,930
<i>If nothing else, 
this is not a sign of hate.</i>

302
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:31,890
I'm sorry for not replying to you 
and avoiding you for so long.

303
00:14:32,550 --> 00:14:35,830
I couldn't stop thinking about Ruka-chan.

304
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:39,110
And I felt bad for her, so I couldn't 
bring myself to get in touch.

305
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:43,450
It's a little belated, but I figured 
it was better than nothing.

306
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:46,410
<i>Mizuhara... You really...</i>

307
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:50,140
<i>Yikes. I feel like I'm about 
to cry for some reason.</i>

308
00:14:51,350 --> 00:14:55,560
So, uh... well, this is an apology?

309
00:14:56,230 --> 00:14:58,460
All I'm doing lately is apologizing.

310
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:02,420
<i>It's now! Now or never!</i>

311
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:08,460
I... I heard from Yaemori-san that 
you were doing it for Ruka-chan.

312
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:10,390
So I don't mind. Not at all.

313
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:13,980
Heck, I've caused you so much trouble,

314
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:16,660
I was worried you were 
down in the dumps over it.

315
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:18,770
So I was kinda relieved when I heard.

316
00:15:19,470 --> 00:15:22,120
I've been wanting to apologize 
to you for everything

317
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:24,040
that happened on the trip, too.

318
00:15:25,370 --> 00:15:27,990
I've been wanting to talk things out.

319
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:30,950
I get it.

320
00:15:31,810 --> 00:15:37,210
I remember what happened in Izu, too, 
and I know you only did it to save my ass.

321
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:37,210
It's not like that was 
the first time, right?

322
00:15:37,750 --> 00:15:44,550
I know I'm out of line saying this, 
and that it's awkward for you to answer.

323
00:15:44,830 --> 00:15:50,820
But I can't help but think that 
that wasn't just you doing your job.

324
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:55,610
I want to ask you straight-up if 
there was more to it than that.

325
00:15:57,180 --> 00:16:01,270
Yaemori-san told me that you were 
working through your feelings, too,

326
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:03,450
so I'm not saying I want 
an answer right away.

327
00:16:04,150 --> 00:16:08,020
But I meant every word 
of what I said back then.

328
00:16:09,150 --> 00:16:14,180
That's the Mizuhara Chizuru 
I've come to love!

329
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:17,200
W-Well, see you.

330
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:20,900
Time's up, huh? Thanks for the date.

331
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:22,880
I'm excited to taste this chocolate.

332
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:25,840
I was really, really happy 
to see you again.

333
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,040
<i>Hold it in, dumbass!</i>

334
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,260
<i>What the hell? My body's giving up!</i>

335
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:35,100
<i>My hands are trembling.</i>

336
00:16:35,100 --> 00:16:38,250
<i>My legs are quivering. 
I'm finding it hard to stand.</i>

337
00:16:39,310 --> 00:16:41,520
<i>Why am I this close to crying?</i>

338
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,920
<i>I don't have it in me to 
hear Mizuhara's response!</i>

339
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,740
<i>I can barely hold it together!</i>

340
00:16:47,550 --> 00:16:51,630
<i>I've had enough for today. 
I said what I needed to say.</i>

341
00:16:51,950 --> 00:16:56,290
<i>I told Mizuhara how I felt.</i>

342
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,040
Wait!

343
00:17:06,630 --> 00:17:08,090
Can I be honest?

344
00:17:12,890 --> 00:17:16,470
<i>Wait, what? Be honest, here and now?</i>

345
00:17:17,070 --> 00:17:22,440
<i>She's gonna say yes or no—
if she likes me or not!</i>

346
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:25,020
Frankly...

347
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:29,740
even I don't know what these feelings are.

348
00:17:31,610 --> 00:17:36,160
<i>"I don't know"? 
Right, that's what Yaemori-san said.</i>

349
00:17:36,590 --> 00:17:40,620
She also said she doesn't know what 
to call the feelings she has for you.

350
00:17:40,990 --> 00:17:43,330
I do realize that it's weird.

351
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:45,600
I'm supposed to be doing my job here,

352
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:49,050
but I'm in so deep that I can't 
talk my way out of it anymore.

353
00:17:49,410 --> 00:17:51,840
And I don't know why I did what I did.

354
00:17:54,550 --> 00:17:58,030
I'll have you know I spent these three 
months trying to figure it out.

355
00:17:58,030 --> 00:18:01,310
If any other clients found out, 
it'd be a huge issue.

356
00:18:01,310 --> 00:18:04,440
And mostly, the way things were 
didn't feel right to me.

357
00:18:04,910 --> 00:18:08,150
I even considered quitting 
this rental girlfriend job.

358
00:18:09,910 --> 00:18:13,570
<i>Quit the rental girlfriend job? 
Who, Mizuhara? Because of me?</i>

359
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:15,320
B-But what about the money?

360
00:18:17,150 --> 00:18:18,280
What about the bills?

361
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,280
That's why you're
doing this, right?

362
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,200
Honestly, it would hurt.

363
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,200
It does put food
on the table

364
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:27,220
This pays well and that helps, 
and I only get a few acting gigs a month.

365
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:28,970
Plus, I like this job.

366
00:18:28,970 --> 00:18:31,040
I could be a hostess or whatever,

367
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:34,260
but I know my way around this, 
and letting it go would be a risk.

368
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:37,800
Y-You can't!

369
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:40,420
I brought all this on.

370
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:44,140
I couldn't take it if you fell 
on your sword because of me.

371
00:18:47,530 --> 00:18:50,070
I'll keep going, if you insist.

372
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:52,900
<i>Cute!</i>

373
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,960
But I'm not going to 
sweep this under the rug.

374
00:18:56,990 --> 00:18:59,990
I don't want to pretend any 
part of my life didn't happen,

375
00:18:59,990 --> 00:19:03,830
and I want to figure out my feelings 
so I'll know how to in the future.

376
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:08,220
Mini-chan told me that 
this is what a real bond is.

377
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:12,050
And it only leads to love, 
as everyone else likes to call it.

378
00:19:13,790 --> 00:19:15,970
<i>Love? Then...</i>

379
00:19:16,470 --> 00:19:17,930
<i>Then her answer is...</i>

380
00:19:18,870 --> 00:19:23,640
But think about it this way. 
It's my job to be loved.

381
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:24,980
Huh?

382
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:27,820
You say you want me to play it natural,

383
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:31,320
but it's not like I'm showing 
100% of my real self.

384
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:33,570
There are definitely parts I'm faking.

385
00:19:33,990 --> 00:19:38,660
Telling me you love that version of me 
just makes me go, "You're okay with that?"

386
00:19:39,550 --> 00:19:40,490
<i>Mizuhara...</i>

387
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:46,520
I mean, you might just be in love 
with "Mizuhara Chizuru," not me.

388
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:55,210
I don't think anyone's capable of 
letting 100% of their true self show.

389
00:19:56,780 --> 00:20:02,350
We're only human. There's always bound 
to be some lies and fakery involved.

390
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,810
Yeah, maybe.

391
00:20:06,710 --> 00:20:12,820
But I can't take that extra step when 
I'm not sure about my own feelings,

392
00:20:12,820 --> 00:20:16,960
and I want to pursue a relationship 
like that only when I know I'm in love.

393
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:23,490
<i>Yeah, she's out of my reach.</i>

394
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:28,540
<i>Ultimately, nothing has changed.</i>

395
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:33,230
<i>Even if I think we've gotten closer, 
we're still rental girlfriend and client.</i>

396
00:20:33,230 --> 00:20:35,210
<i>I can work up all the courage in the world,</i>

397
00:20:35,210 --> 00:20:37,680
<i>and my feelings still won't get through to her.</i>

398
00:20:38,230 --> 00:20:42,060
<i>It's not fair, Mizuhara. 
Did we start off on the wrong foot?</i>

399
00:20:42,060 --> 00:20:45,930
<i>If we'd met under normal circumstances, 
would things have turned out differently?</i>

400
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:50,060
<i>But I can't go back and change that.</i>

401
00:20:50,690 --> 00:20:52,480
<i>A kiss doesn't change anything.</i>

402
00:20:53,550 --> 00:20:57,070
<i>Mizuhara will never be mine...</i>

403
00:21:03,030 --> 00:21:07,160
So, uh, I want you to give me 
just a little more time.

404
00:21:10,030 --> 00:21:13,130
Huh? Mizuhara, you mean...

405
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:18,030
I want to know, too.

406
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:20,800
I've never felt this before, 
and I want to know what it is.

407
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:25,720
So, hey...

408
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:31,310
I'm going to look into it.

409
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:36,950
Anyway, I had fun today. Thank you.

410
00:21:36,950 --> 00:21:37,730
Bye.

411
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:59,920
Today

412
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:59,920
Ichinose Chizuru

413
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:59,920
Thanks for telling me about the yoga pamphlet.
I'll go pick it up sometime soon, so hold on
to it for me?

414
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:04,840
"Thanks, bud!"

415
00:22:13,230 --> 00:22:14,980
Read

416
00:22:13,230 --> 00:22:14,980
Gotcha!

417
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:20,500
<i>My memories are fuzzy 
on what happened after that.</i>

418
00:23:20,990 --> 00:23:27,340
<i>But I do remember that I actually walked 
two and a half hours home from Harajuku.</i>

419
00:23:27,750 --> 00:23:33,180
<i>The entire way back, I held myself 
back from exploding with joy.</i>

420
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:28,800
Whoa, that guy.

421
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:30,220
He's power walking.

422
00:23:34,070 --> 00:23:35,100
<i>And lastly...</i>

423
00:23:45,590 --> 00:23:48,820
<i>Once I made it back to Nerima 
and got away from the crowd,</i>

424
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:51,410
<i>I couldn't hold it in anymore.</i>

425
00:23:57,390 --> 00:24:01,250
Rawr! Mizuhara gave me chocolate!

426
00:24:01,250 --> 00:24:02,550
Woohoo!

427
00:24:02,550 --> 00:24:05,840
Hey! You're being too loud 
over just some chocolate.

428
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:09,780
No, this is not just some chocolate.

429
00:24:09,780 --> 00:24:13,320
It's chocolate that you gave me!

430
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:15,300
Okay, okay, settle down.

431
00:24:15,300 --> 00:24:16,940
Now, next time on <i>Rent-a-Girlfriend</i>:

432
00:24:16,940 --> 00:24:17,940
"Investigation and...

433
00:24:17,940 --> 00:24:18,450
...Girlfriend."

434
00:24:18,450 --> 00:24:22,730
I'm going out for another run! Grawr!

435
00:24:22,730 --> 00:24:24,860
Hey! Wow, he actually went!

436
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:27,030
"Investigation and Girlfriend"

437
00:24:24,860 --> 00:24:26,650
It made him that happy?

